1
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:35,000
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,920
[Episode 18]

3
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,789
Chen Kailai,

4
00:01:39,509 --> 00:01:42,070
for your contribution
to eliminating Communist spies,

5
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,590
you are awarded a medal.

6
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:07,650
Seeing you get rewarded

7
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:11,250
makes me happier
than getting rewarded myself.

8
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,590
Why?

9
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:15,840
Because I'm your mentor.

10
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,040
I got credit because of your influence.

11
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:20,829
How can I face others in the future?

12
00:02:20,829 --> 00:02:21,829
I have my pride.

13
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,390
You know what?

14
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,260
Favors are more fragile than your pride.

15
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,350
With this bronze medal,

16
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:34,800
you'll have

17
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:37,310
a bright future at No. 76.

18
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:40,870
I'm just a photographer.

19
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,120
Why do I need that?

20
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,000
People live for a bright future.

21
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:45,900
Otherwise,

22
00:02:46,329 --> 00:02:47,730
it's just a waste of time.

23
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:51,840
Look.

24
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,190
Only the dead don't need it.

25
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:10,830
Come on in.

26
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:38,210
Leifeng Pagoda...

27
00:03:44,150 --> 00:03:46,210
Leifeng Pagoda sacrificed himself.

28
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:01,160
It's not easy
for two people to come together.

29
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,390
There are some things

30
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,440
you should tell her sooner.

31
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:12,560
I'll tell her when she returns safely.

32
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:16,380
If I'd known it was the last time
we'd meet,

33
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,260
I would've asked him to stay for a meal.

34
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,390
He loved you.

35
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,560
He loved his ideals

36
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,000
and faith.

37
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,250
I'm ready.

38
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,240
I will die too.

39
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,170
You must stay alive.

40
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:23,780
For him,

41
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,000
and for yourself.

42
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:24,870
Newspapers!

43
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:26,460
Newspapers!

44
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:28,340
Newspapers!

45
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,250
I've found Du Huangqiao's place.

46
00:06:35,070 --> 00:06:36,400
What are you going to do?

47
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:37,510
Kill him.

48
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:40,540
To avenge Zhao Qian?

49
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,340
He'll make a move on you sooner or later.

50
00:06:44,870 --> 00:06:46,870
Now is not a good time to strike.

51
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:49,540
We can give the address
to the Hurricane Team.

52
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:50,140
Enough.

53
00:06:54,070 --> 00:06:56,800
We came all the way
from the Northeast to Nanjing.

54
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,780
All this time,

55
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:01,780
it wasn't just to kill Du Huangqiao.

56
00:07:35,909 --> 00:07:37,180
You bastards!

57
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:06,980
The comrades around us

58
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:10,900
have left us one by one.

59
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,430
Fortunately,

60
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,500
you've always been here.

61
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:27,700
I won't allow you to leave before me.

62
00:08:57,570 --> 00:08:59,100
I look so ugly in this photo.

63
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:02,490
Not just ugly.

64
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:04,900
This photo

65
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:06,910
might cost you your life.

66
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,220
You only have one way out now.

67
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:13,640
What is it?

68
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:15,820
Become my man.

69
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:17,220
What?

70
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,270
Become one of us.

71
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:33,390
If you don't agree,

72
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:36,840
it'll be hard for me to save your life.

73
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,740
Tao Dachun could kill you at any moment

74
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:43,620
for being a traitor.

75
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,580
I'm not a traitor.

76
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,350
That's not up to you.

77
00:09:51,610 --> 00:09:53,800
That's a label Du Huangqiao put on me!

78
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:56,540
Do you remember Shasha,

79
00:09:57,690 --> 00:09:58,950
who helped you before?

80
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:02,010
That bastard Du Huangqiao

81
00:10:02,910 --> 00:10:04,840
sent several men to gang-rape her,

82
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,180
driving her to her death.

83
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:13,870
Let go of me!

84
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,670
Let go of me!

85
00:10:17,890 --> 00:10:20,290
Get out! Don't touch me!

86
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:35,290
Cang Guanglian,

87
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:37,860
you liar.

88
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:42,440
You said you'd take care of me
for the rest of my life.

89
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:03,710
He did that?

90
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:05,480
I told you before

91
00:11:06,850 --> 00:11:09,780
that staying with this kind of person
won't end well.

92
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:13,470
Unless...

93
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,250
you become mine.

94
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,170
That's the only way you'll stay alive.

95
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:36,860
Alright, I agree.

96
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,540
That's more like it.

97
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:53,000
What do you need me to do?

98
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,440
The Japanese have a project.

99
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,030
What is it?

100
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:01,630
It's called Project Slumber.

101
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:05,910
Is it the one related to Ishida?

102
00:12:07,790 --> 00:12:08,430
Yes.

103
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:12,310
Ishida is dead.

104
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:15,020
I don't know any other Japanese.

105
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,650
Su Men and Du Huangqiao

106
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,240
both have connections with the Japanese.

107
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,570
You just need to stay by their side

108
00:12:23,570 --> 00:12:24,970
and gather information.

109
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:26,650
Remember,

110
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,440
don't mess around.

111
00:12:29,050 --> 00:12:31,450
Staying alive is the most important thing.

112
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:03,220
Hello.

113
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:04,190
Director Li,

114
00:13:05,010 --> 00:13:07,090
I heard some bad news about you.

115
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:08,820
Tell me.

116
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:13,500
[Asami Sawa,
Japanese Plum Blossom Agency Agent]

117
00:13:11,390 --> 00:13:13,460
They found Yu Yingxiang's ledger.

118
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,600
Who did it?

119
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,260
That woman from Nanjing.

120
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:29,340
What is this?

121
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:33,060
The negatives of the photos
I took of you last time.

122
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:35,660
Also...

123
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:37,930
I promised Jinbao

124
00:13:38,550 --> 00:13:40,810
to keep an eye on Project Slumber for her.

125
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:42,830
Maybe this way I can learn something

126
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:44,860
about the NBIS's movements.

127
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,230
That's a good thing.

128
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:52,990
The Hurricane Team
won't try to kill you anymore.

129
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:57,170
But you need to be more careful
in the future.

130
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,530
You'll be playing 3 roles at once.

131
00:14:00,950 --> 00:14:01,590
I know.

132
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:03,550
But only one of them

133
00:14:04,070 --> 00:14:05,070
is the real me.

134
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:06,580
No.

135
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,110
You must bear in mind

136
00:14:08,350 --> 00:14:09,610
that all three are you.

137
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:11,570
That's how you play them well.

138
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:25,550
Su Causeway is leaving.

139
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:27,980
Go say goodbye to her.

140
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:00,220
Sister.

141
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:10,030
Long time no see.

142
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:12,860
We will meet again.

143
00:15:15,010 --> 00:15:17,140
Someone once said we would meet again,

144
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,500
but I never saw him again.

145
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:22,830
So this time,

146
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:24,790
I don't want to say that.

147
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:28,970
If we never meet again,

148
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,690
just remember the past.

149
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,200
The future is unknown.

150
00:15:36,630 --> 00:15:38,430
I will remember you as you are now

151
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:40,450
and think of you as you were.

152
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:43,840
What we're doing now

153
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,680
is for the future.

154
00:15:47,390 --> 00:15:49,250
Then we will definitely succeed.

155
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,610
Let me take a picture of you.

156
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,330
Why take a picture of me?

157
00:15:57,510 --> 00:15:58,440
Your camera

158
00:15:58,530 --> 00:16:01,430
should capture
the most beautiful things in the world.

159
00:16:01,430 --> 00:16:04,120
What is "all the beauty in the world"?

160
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,990
The most beautiful thing

161
00:16:07,870 --> 00:16:08,720
is peace.

162
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:10,690
I remember.

163
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,080
The most beautiful thing

164
00:16:13,710 --> 00:16:14,630
is peace.

165
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:42,870
Sister!

166
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:44,270
Sister!

167
00:16:44,990 --> 00:16:45,920
Wait for me!

168
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:46,960
Sister!

169
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,040
Sister!

170
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,320
Wait for me!

171
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:50,630
Wait for me!

172
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:55,550
If you leave now,

173
00:16:55,550 --> 00:16:56,580
what about the wedding?

174
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,840
That's not what I want.

175
00:16:57,990 --> 00:16:59,590
I want to make my own choices.

176
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,920
Where are you going?

177
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:01,720
I don't know!

178
00:17:01,870 --> 00:17:03,080
Will you come back?

179
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,510
Thank you!

180
00:17:06,750 --> 00:17:08,270
Where can I find you?

181
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:33,550
We can't keep Su Men around anymore.

182
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:37,510
She is protected
by the Japanese and Nanjing.

183
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:38,840
Confronting her openly

184
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:41,640
might leave us vulnerable.

185
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:51,750
Then let's use someone else to do it.

186
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,880
The tickets are booked.

187
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,410
We're leaving for Nanjing
tomorrow morning.

188
00:18:01,230 --> 00:18:01,880
Got it.

189
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:03,810
Come in.

190
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:10,860
How are the preparations?

191
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,470
Boss.

192
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,510
I've even thought of
the headline for tomorrow's tabloid.

193
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,580
It will be called "A Tragic Beauty:

194
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:19,770
Nanjing Inspector Shot Dead by Bandit."

195
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:23,270
Good.

196
00:18:26,950 --> 00:18:27,810
Then tomorrow,

197
00:18:28,950 --> 00:18:31,080
I'll have to buy a few more newspapers.

198
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:31,970
Okay, boss.

199
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:50,180
Inspector Su.

200
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:10,860
General Kagesa,

201
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:13,060
may I have this dance?

202
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:18,560
Yes,

203
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:20,280
you may.

204
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:27,620
Du Huangqiao is acting weird today.

205
00:19:30,610 --> 00:19:31,410
What's wrong?

206
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:32,990
I heard him say,

207
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,410
"Nanjing Inspector

208
00:19:34,850 --> 00:19:36,080
Shot Dead by Bandit."

209
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:37,450
Be careful.

210
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:56,780
Captain Du.

211
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:06,980
The Green Gang has an operation
in the French Concession tonight.

212
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,220
They are coming for me.

213
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:24,480
Go home now

214
00:20:24,850 --> 00:20:25,910
and move the stuff.

215
00:20:28,650 --> 00:20:29,520
What about you?

216
00:20:31,150 --> 00:20:31,910
Go quickly.

217
00:20:42,650 --> 00:20:43,650
Follow Cui Enxi.

218
00:20:43,970 --> 00:20:44,540
Yes.

219
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,200
-Director Li.
-Director Li.

220
00:21:15,610 --> 00:21:16,470
How is it going?

221
00:21:17,890 --> 00:21:19,090
Everything is ready.

222
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:33,170
Inspector Su,
you're usually the first to leave.

223
00:21:33,170 --> 00:21:35,620
You seem to be in high spirits today.

224
00:21:38,410 --> 00:21:40,140
I can't always spoil the fun.

225
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,480
However,

226
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:52,670
Detective Su's dance pool can shine brightly.

227
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,130
We've known each other for so long,

228
00:21:56,130 --> 00:21:56,930
yet I...

229
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,450
have never danced with you.

230
00:22:05,370 --> 00:22:08,090
It's because you have never invited me.

231
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:12,690
Please.

232
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:29,040
It's because you're too noble,

233
00:22:29,710 --> 00:22:32,040
and a blind man like me
isn't worthy of you.

234
00:22:33,130 --> 00:22:35,330
Then who gave you the courage this time?

235
00:22:39,010 --> 00:22:39,900
Mr. Zhao.

236
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,160
It was Mr. Zhao who told me

237
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:50,080
that life is unpredictable,

238
00:22:51,530 --> 00:22:54,330
all is vanity,

239
00:22:55,210 --> 00:22:58,490
and one must enjoy life while they can.

240
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:02,810
Captain Du, you're a nostalgic person.

241
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,940
Aren't you, Inspector Su?

242
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:09,930
Nostalgia easily breaks one's heart.

243
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,800
Since Mr. Zhao is no longer with us,

244
00:23:14,630 --> 00:23:15,890
I'll be bold enough...

245
00:23:18,150 --> 00:23:20,180
to escort you home.

246
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,160
Don't bother.

247
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,280
I think it's better for you

248
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:28,560
to find a dancing girl.

249
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:39,780
Move!

250
00:23:39,810 --> 00:23:41,140
Move! Get out of the way!

251
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,040
Ms. Su Men.

252
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:47,480
We suspect you

253
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:49,760
are involved
in a case we are investigating.

254
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:51,240
Please come with us.

255
00:23:55,230 --> 00:23:56,030
Detective.

256
00:23:57,450 --> 00:23:59,760
This is No. 76's turf.

257
00:24:00,130 --> 00:24:02,000
What kind of huge case is it

258
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,880
that you need
to take our Inspector Su away?

259
00:24:06,370 --> 00:24:07,130
Captain Du,

260
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:09,580
I am investigating under orders.

261
00:24:09,690 --> 00:24:10,560
No comment.

262
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:18,610
Let's go.

263
00:24:19,820 --> 00:24:20,750
I'll cooperate.

264
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,000
Move, move!

265
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:51,600
Continue!

266
00:24:59,890 --> 00:25:00,890
What should we do?

267
00:25:01,690 --> 00:25:03,890
She already knows about our operation.

268
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:06,340
We can't leave her alive.

269
00:28:18,150 --> 00:28:19,520
Come on, charge over!

270
00:30:42,050 --> 00:30:47,210
♪ This road is so very long ♪

271
00:30:44,130 --> 00:30:45,680
I'm your bodyguard.

272
00:30:46,370 --> 00:30:47,820
I'll protect you from now on.

273
00:30:47,820 --> 00:30:54,590
♪ I don't seem to have done enough ♪

274
00:30:53,250 --> 00:30:54,340
Go!

275
00:30:56,290 --> 00:31:00,820
♪ I follow the warmth
of a heart held close ♪

276
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:58,970
Go!

277
00:31:02,980 --> 00:31:08,840
♪ Moving on without looking back ♪

278
00:31:10,350 --> 00:31:15,580
♪ I have so many things to tell you ♪

279
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:19,080
♪ But I don't think I can give you ♪

280
00:31:19,100 --> 00:31:22,040
♪ The answer you want ♪

281
00:31:23,050 --> 00:31:25,790
♪ Don't let yourself grieve too much ♪

282
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:30,290
♪ When you wake,
the sun will shine again ♪

283
00:31:31,250 --> 00:31:38,750
♪ At the end of the road,
I'll be facing the way we came from ♪

284
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:46,610
♪ This love, to you and me ♪

285
00:31:47,340 --> 00:31:50,090
♪ Is as light is to the night ♪

286
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:55,200
♪ And it brings me hope ♪

287
00:31:55,810 --> 00:32:01,450
♪ There is nowhere left
for darkness to hide ♪

288
00:32:01,690 --> 00:32:03,000
It'll be too late if we don't leave now!

289
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:10,820
♪ Dawn will find its way to your side ♪

290
00:32:12,110 --> 00:32:15,860
♪ And it will never fade away ♪

291
00:32:12,850 --> 00:32:13,720
Get in the car!

292
00:32:31,500 --> 00:32:37,320
♪ Come, tell me what you have to say ♪

293
00:32:37,340 --> 00:32:39,090
♪ And I know your answers ♪

294
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:43,540
♪ Won't change much for me ♪

295
00:32:44,330 --> 00:32:47,300
♪ I have dreams of my own ♪

296
00:32:47,810 --> 00:32:51,720
♪ Like the rising sun ♪

297
00:32:52,440 --> 00:33:01,290
♪ They're in the distance
and in my heart ♪

298
00:33:01,690 --> 00:33:07,840
♪ This love, to you and me ♪

299
00:33:08,630 --> 00:33:11,540
♪ Is as light is to the night ♪

300
00:33:12,140 --> 00:33:16,390
♪ It once gave me hope ♪

301
00:33:16,750 --> 00:33:23,070
♪ There is nowhere left
for darkness to hide ♪

302
00:33:23,430 --> 00:33:29,780
♪ Dawn will find its way to your side ♪

303
00:33:30,110 --> 00:33:35,950
♪ This love, to you and me ♪

304
00:33:36,730 --> 00:33:39,370
♪ Is as light is to the night ♪

305
00:33:40,170 --> 00:33:44,870
♪ It gives me endless hope ♪

306
00:33:45,180 --> 00:33:52,360
♪ There is nowhere left
for darkness to hide ♪

307
00:33:52,380 --> 00:33:59,900
♪ Dawn will find its way to your side ♪

308
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:04,730
♪ It won't fade away ♪

309
00:34:08,560 --> 00:34:13,650
♪ It will always be by your side ♪

310
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:29,850
Boss.

311
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,120
Cui Enxi is dead.

312
00:34:32,889 --> 00:34:34,290
The ledger was not on her.

313
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:39,409
Why don't you die?

314
00:34:48,250 --> 00:34:49,560
I will die for you.

315
00:34:53,770 --> 00:34:55,120
With a face like yours,

316
00:34:55,150 --> 00:34:57,950
no wonder your wife
is still willing to be with you.

317
00:34:58,780 --> 00:34:59,560
Captain Du.

318
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:10,160
Everything in the safe has been taken out.

319
00:35:10,160 --> 00:35:11,290
No ledger was found.

320
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:27,000
At least it wasn't a wasted trip.

321
00:35:31,820 --> 00:35:32,410
Here.

322
00:35:34,210 --> 00:35:35,270
Give it to the boys.

323
00:35:35,700 --> 00:35:36,830
Thank you, Captain.

324
00:35:37,250 --> 00:35:38,680
We didn't find the ledger.

325
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,730
How do we explain this to Director Li?

326
00:35:40,730 --> 00:35:41,850
If I counted on you,

327
00:35:41,970 --> 00:35:43,830
I would have died many times over.

328
00:36:34,210 --> 00:36:35,270
The ledger is gone.

329
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:38,440
But Su Men is still alive.

330
00:36:41,810 --> 00:36:43,890
I want to shut her up forever.

331
00:36:45,290 --> 00:36:47,690
The temporary detention
is only for 2 days.

332
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:51,250
As long as we get the evidence
of Su Men colluding with the Communists,

333
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:53,650
even Hua Liang
won't be able to protect her.

334
00:37:42,330 --> 00:37:43,250
You are Korean?

335
00:37:48,970 --> 00:37:50,370
If you have nowhere to go,

336
00:37:52,610 --> 00:37:53,940
stay with me from now on.

337
00:37:59,470 --> 00:38:00,630
You are pretty.

338
00:38:01,580 --> 00:38:03,180
I'll protect you from now on.

339
00:38:22,850 --> 00:38:24,110
Have a bowl of wontons.

340
00:38:24,810 --> 00:38:26,270
You haven't eaten all day.

341
00:38:31,850 --> 00:38:33,120
I want them...

342
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:36,980
to pay in blood.

343
00:38:42,600 --> 00:38:44,460
Is there anything I can help with?

344
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:50,950
Here.

345
00:38:53,450 --> 00:38:54,560
This thing.

346
00:38:54,640 --> 00:38:55,730
Captain Du said

347
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:59,880
this is the evidence of Su Men
colluding with the Communists.

348
00:39:01,450 --> 00:39:03,580
Isn't this a little too half-hearted?

349
00:39:04,040 --> 00:39:05,900
You messed up her house like this.

350
00:39:06,250 --> 00:39:08,050
You know Inspector Su's temper.

351
00:39:08,200 --> 00:39:09,890
She may settle the score with you
after this.

352
00:39:09,890 --> 00:39:11,150
What are you thinking?

353
00:39:12,330 --> 00:39:14,120
Colluding with the Communists.

354
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,200
Su Men is

355
00:39:15,650 --> 00:39:17,450
completely finished this time.

356
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:20,930
Why didn't you come yesterday?

357
00:39:20,930 --> 00:39:23,260
There were a lot of good things yesterday.

358
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:26,340
Alright. Go ahead and take the pictures.

359
00:39:36,170 --> 00:39:37,110
Raise your glasses!

360
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:37,840
And you guys.

361
00:39:38,090 --> 00:39:38,700
Cheers!

362
00:39:38,730 --> 00:39:39,250
Come on!

363
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:40,770
Director.

364
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:47,340
Chen Kailai, what brings you here?

365
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:49,600
I'm here to deliver some photos.

366
00:39:49,930 --> 00:39:51,160
I have an idea.

367
00:39:51,810 --> 00:39:53,270
You teach me photography,

368
00:39:53,330 --> 00:39:54,680
and I'll teach you how to do pedicures.

369
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:55,200
What do you think?

370
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,460
Pedicures? Forget it.

371
00:39:56,850 --> 00:39:57,650
Director Li.

372
00:40:04,770 --> 00:40:06,700
You use your art to serve your work.

373
00:40:07,160 --> 00:40:08,040
Well done.

374
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:09,970
Good job.

375
00:40:10,680 --> 00:40:11,290
Sit here.

376
00:40:11,290 --> 00:40:12,420
I'll be leaving now.

377
00:40:12,860 --> 00:40:13,450
Sit.

378
00:40:17,290 --> 00:40:18,480
Danni, come here.

379
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:20,380
Keep my bro company.

380
00:40:20,640 --> 00:40:21,370
Okay.

381
00:40:22,250 --> 00:40:23,520
Let's go dance.

382
00:40:23,520 --> 00:40:24,450
I don't know how.

383
00:40:24,860 --> 00:40:25,340
Come on.

384
00:40:25,370 --> 00:40:26,380
I... I really don't know how.

385
00:40:26,380 --> 00:40:27,380
I'll teach you.

386
00:40:27,410 --> 00:40:28,370
No, thanks.

387
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:30,310
Then let's have a drink.

388
00:40:30,310 --> 00:40:31,310
I can't drink.

389
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:34,000
I got some news from the Japanese.

390
00:40:34,480 --> 00:40:36,610
That woman will be released tomorrow.

391
00:40:41,770 --> 00:40:42,700
You are so drunk?

392
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:45,370
Be careful.

393
00:40:48,410 --> 00:40:50,740
I heard something happened at Paramount.

394
00:40:52,290 --> 00:40:53,250
I remember

395
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:57,500
the first time
I met Inspector Su on the train.

396
00:40:59,120 --> 00:41:00,120
She saved me.

397
00:41:02,850 --> 00:41:05,050
I didn't expect someone so influential

398
00:41:06,080 --> 00:41:07,210
to get into trouble.

399
00:41:09,470 --> 00:41:11,870
Why are you feeling sorry
for that traitor?

400
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:14,540
Don't tell me you like that demoness.

401
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:18,610
From Li Musheng's death until now,

402
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:22,810
it feels

403
00:41:23,810 --> 00:41:25,160
like a lifetime.

404
00:41:28,330 --> 00:41:29,370
My cousin,

405
00:41:30,480 --> 00:41:31,520
Mr. Zhao,

406
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:33,000
Auntie—

407
00:41:34,370 --> 00:41:35,370
they all came

408
00:41:38,770 --> 00:41:39,680
and left.

409
00:41:43,450 --> 00:41:45,560
I feel like I'm living

410
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:48,770
in a movie,

411
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:50,970
or...

412
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:56,110
a fading photograph.

413
00:42:00,890 --> 00:42:02,550
I think you've lost your mind.

414
00:42:02,970 --> 00:42:04,450
Save your sympathy.

415
00:42:05,040 --> 00:42:05,970
Sooner or later,

416
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:07,040
I will die too.

417
00:42:11,850 --> 00:42:13,580
Don't forget you are my man now.

418
00:42:13,600 --> 00:42:15,250
You could get a mission at any time.

419
00:42:15,250 --> 00:42:17,580
There's no time for you to be sentimental.

420
00:42:33,150 --> 00:42:34,240
They're all gone.

421
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:39,080
Who am I supposed to contact?

422
00:42:50,930 --> 00:42:51,600
Hello?

423
00:42:51,850 --> 00:42:53,330
Is this Fulai Photo Studio?

424
00:42:53,330 --> 00:42:54,560
May I speak to Mr. Chen?

425
00:42:54,560 --> 00:42:55,330
Speaking.

426
00:42:56,290 --> 00:42:59,410
Would it be convenient for you
to send over

427
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:02,120
the photos Ms. Su took at your place?

428
00:43:03,160 --> 00:43:03,770
Who did you say?
